    <!--
        DISPOSITION BA GAP CLOSURE - TRANCHE 2 ONLY (Sell Meter / Home page).
        Built 2026-08-31 for agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t2-design.md.

        WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. manifest/package.xml is the FULL-ORG RETRIEVE manifest (82 type
        blocks); a source-dir deploy of force-app has the same problem. Either would sweep several
        OTHER concurrent streams' undeployed, unreviewed work into usman-dpeg. Non-Tranche-2 work
        confirmed present in this shared working tree at build time:
          permissionsets  DPEG_Task_Edit, DPEG_Checklist_Edit, DPEG_Checklist_View,
                          Transaction_Prereq_Override_Access, DPEG_Transaction_Edit/_View
          customPermissions  Transaction_Prereq_Override
          classes         BrokerProtectionConfigSelector(+Test)
          objects         Transaction__c.Tasks_Open__c, Activity.Blocked_By__c,
                          Activity.Is_Prerequisite_Met__c, Activity validationRules
          flows           Transaction_Stage_Closed_Sets_Status
          reports         Transactions/Total_Open_Tasks, Total_Completed_Tasks
        None of it is listed below. Nothing is wildcarded - a wildcard re-introduces the sweep.

        DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, though modified in the tree:
        - reports/Dispositions/Total_Argus_Value - the T2 edit is a COMMENT ONLY. Deploying a
          Report has no org value here and carries a real risk of overwriting a UI-side edit.
        - permissionsets/DPEG_Admin_Access - its change belongs to TRANCHE 1 and is already live
          (deploy 0Afiw000000UCLVCA4, 2026-08-31 14:18 UTC).
        - scripts/** - anonymous Apex, not deployable metadata.
        - Every Tranche 1 component. All are already deployed; re-shipping them would widen the
          blast radius of this deploy for no gain.

        DEPLOY ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING AND FAILS SILENTLY IF INVERTED.
        CustomField + CustomPermission must land no later than the PermissionSets. A
        customPermissions entry naming a permission the org does not hold fails the deploy of the
        WHOLE permission set; a field with no FLS aborts the entire DML statement rather than
        degrading. Shipping the Apex WITHOUT the permission-set grant is the worst case: it denies
        every principal silently - disabled button everywhere, server refuses every YELLOW create,
        no error anywhere. One package keeps all of it in one transaction.

        PERMISSION SETS REPLACE, THEY DO NOT MERGE. Both sets below were reconciled against the
        live org by SOQL across FieldPermissions + ObjectPermissions + SetupEntityAccess and
        showed ZERO org-only grants. That third read is not optional: Disposition_Deal_Actions on
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit is invisible to the first two. Re-run the three-way reconciliation
        immediately before deploying - the org is being modified by other streams today.
    -->

